#
# Root certificates that Mozilla retired by age (not for compromise) and that
# certifi therefore no longer ships, but that big hosting providers still sit
# under through cross-signed certificates. gen_assets.py adds them to the
# firmware's CA bundle.
#
# Why this matters on the ESP32: its bundle check (esp_crt_bundle) looks up
# only the issuer of the LAST certificate the server sends. A browser would
# find another path to a current root; the ESP32 can't, so when the chain
# ends in a cross-signed certificate the device needs the old root too.
# (2026.10.7.3 device logs: adsb.fi and airplanes.live failed with "Failed to
# verify certificate" / X509 fatal error -12288.)
#
# Each certificate below is from certifi 2024.8.30 (PyPI). Its SHA-256
# fingerprint is checked by gen_assets.py.

